@page "/about"

<div class="container-fluid">
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-12">
            <h1 class="mb-4">About the Ruffin Weather Station</h1>
            
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-lg-8">
                    <div class="card mb-4">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h3 class="card-title">🌦️ How This All Started</h3>
                            <p class="card-text">
                                So my kids brought home a little DIY no-tech weather station from school and asked me to help them build it. 
                                I'm always excited about any opportunity to geek out with them, so we spent about 20 minutes building 
                                the thing and then a week or so collecting data in an Excel spreadsheet.
                            </p>
                            <p class="card-text">
                                That's when we decided to take things to the next level and build one of our own. This is a super popular 
                                project, so there are tons of resources available online. I ended up buying the SparkFun Weather Station Kit 
                                (which includes all the mechanical sensors - weather vane, anemometer, rain gauge) and a "Weather HAT" from 
                                Pimoroni with digital sensors for humidity, temperature, light levels, and barometric pressure.
                            </p>
                            <p class="card-text">
                                The fun part was writing code to read the sensor data and pipe it to an app. What started as a simple 
                                family project has turned into this full-featured weather monitoring system. The hat arrived and suddenly 
                                I found myself way more interested in this project than anything I had going on at work!
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="card mb-4">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h3 class="card-title">🔧 The Technical Stuff</h3>
                            <p class="card-text">
                                Here's what I ended up putting together. It's basically a Raspberry Pi doing all the heavy lifting - 
                                collecting data from the sensors and transmitting it to this web dashboard where we can see real-time 
                                conditions and analyze trends over time.
                            </p>
                            <div class="row">
                                <div class="col-md-6">
                                    <h5>Hardware:</h5>
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>Raspberry Pi (the brain of the operation)</li>
                                        <li>SparkFun Weather Station Kit</li>
                                        <li>Pimoroni Weather HAT</li>
                                        <li>A bunch of sensors for everything you'd want to measure</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                                <div class="col-md-6">
                                    <h5>Software:</h5>
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>ASP.NET Core Blazor (this dashboard you're looking at)</li>
                                        <li>Python code running on the Pi</li>
                                        <li>RESTful API to tie it all together</li>
                                        <li>Some AI magic for weather predictions</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                
                <div class="col-lg-4">
                    <div class="card mb-4">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h3 class="card-title">📊 What We're Tracking</h3>
                            <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
                                <li class="list-group-item d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
                                    Temperature
                                    <span class="badge bg-primary rounded-pill">°C/°F</span>
                                </li>
                                <li class="list-group-item d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
                                    Humidity
                                    <span class="badge bg-primary rounded-pill">%</span>
                                </li>
                                <li class="list-group-item d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
                                    Barometric Pressure
                                    <span class="badge bg-primary rounded-pill">hPa</span>
                                </li>
                                <li class="list-group-item d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
                                    Wind Speed & Direction
                                    <span class="badge bg-primary rounded-pill">m/s</span>
                                </li>
                                <li class="list-group-item d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
                                    Rainfall
                                    <span class="badge bg-primary rounded-pill">mm</span>
                                </li>
                                <li class="list-group-item d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
                                    Light Levels
                                    <span class="badge bg-primary rounded-pill">lux</span>
                                </li>
                                <li class="list-group-item d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
                                    Dewpoint
                                    <span class="badge bg-primary rounded-pill">°C</span>
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="card">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h3 class="card-title">🚀 What It Does</h3>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Collects data 24/7 (when the Pi stays plugged in)</li>
                                <li>Shows historical trends and analysis</li>
                                <li>AI-powered predictions (because why not?)</li>
                                <li>Interactive charts that actually work</li>
                                <li>Weather notes for when something interesting happens</li>
                                <li>Works on your phone (responsive design FTW)</li>
                                <li>Shows times in your timezone, not mine</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="row mt-4">
                <div class="col-12">
                    <div class="card">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h3 class="card-title">📖 The Full Story</h3>
                            <p class="card-text">
                                This project has been an incredible learning experience. It combines hardware tinkering, software development, 
                                and data science in ways I didn't expect when we started. What began as helping my kids with a school project 
                                turned into something much more sophisticated and useful.
                            </p>
                            <p class="card-text">
                                If you want the full story of how this all came together (including the technical challenges and moments of 
                                frustration when things didn't work), you can read the blog post that started it all:
                            </p>
                            <a href="https://zachruffin.com/writing-words-about-things/building-a-weather-station" 
                               class="btn btn-primary me-2 mb-2" target="_blank">
                                <i class="bi bi-arrow-up-right-square"></i> Read the Full Story
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="row mt-4">
                <div class="col-12">
                    <div class="card">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h3 class="card-title">💻 The Code (For Fellow Nerds)</h3>
                            <p class="card-text">
                                This project is actually made up of several different repositories. I've made everything open source 
                                because I remember how helpful it was to find examples when I was figuring this stuff out. 
                                Feel free to poke around, copy whatever's useful, or let me know if you find bugs!
                            </p>
                            
                            <div class="row">
                                <div class="col-md-4 mb-3">
                                    <div class="card h-100 border-secondary">
                                        <div class="card-body">
                                            <h5 class="card-title">
                                                <i class="bi bi-globe"></i> This Website
                                            </h5>
                                            <p class="card-text">
                                                The Blazor dashboard you're looking at right now. I built it with ASP.NET Core 
                                                and it handles all the real-time data visualization and AI predictions.
                                            </p>
                                            <div class="mb-2">
                                                <span class="badge bg-secondary me-1">Blazor</span>
                                                <span class="badge bg-secondary me-1">C#</span>
                                                <span class="badge bg-secondary">.NET</span>
                                            </div>
                                            <a href="https://github.com/faintdeception/RuffinWeatherStation" 
                                               class="btn btn-outline-primary" target="_blank">
                                                <i class="bi bi-github"></i> View on GitHub
                                            </a>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                
                                <div class="col-md-4 mb-3">
                                    <div class="card h-100 border-secondary">
                                        <div class="card-body">
                                            <h5 class="card-title">
                                                <i class="bi bi-cpu"></i> The Raspberry Pi Code
                                            </h5>
                                            <p class="card-text">
                                                The Python code that runs on the Raspberry Pi. It reads all the sensor data 
                                                and sends it to the web dashboard. This is where the magic happens.
                                            </p>
                                            <div class="mb-2">
                                                <span class="badge bg-secondary me-1">Python</span>
                                                <span class="badge bg-secondary me-1">Raspberry Pi</span>
                                                <span class="badge bg-secondary">IoT</span>
                                            </div>
                                            <a href="https://github.com/faintdeception/weather-station" 
                                               class="btn btn-outline-primary" target="_blank">
                                                <i class="bi bi-github"></i> View on GitHub
                                            </a>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                
                                <div class="col-md-4 mb-3">
                                    <div class="card h-100 border-secondary">
                                        <div class="card-body">
                                            <h5 class="card-title">
                                                <i class="bi bi-robot"></i> The AI Predictions
                                            </h5>
                                            <p class="card-text">
                                                The machine learning service that tries to predict the weather based on historical data. 
                                                Sometimes it's surprisingly accurate, sometimes... well, it's still learning.
                                            </p>
                                            <div class="mb-2">
                                                <span class="badge bg-secondary me-1">Python</span>
                                                <span class="badge bg-secondary me-1">AI/ML</span>
                                                <span class="badge bg-secondary">LLM</span>
                                            </div>
                                            <a href="https://github.com/faintdeception/weather-llm-service" 
                                               class="btn btn-outline-primary" target="_blank">
                                                <i class="bi bi-github"></i> View on GitHub
                                            </a>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            
                            <div class="alert alert-info mt-3">
                                <i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i>
                                <strong>Open Source:</strong> All of this code is available for anyone to use, learn from, or improve upon. 
                                If you find something useful or spot a bug, don't hesitate to fork it or submit a pull request!
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
